#: ../../source/docs/common-auxiliary-functions.rst:5
#: 8ca604d5cb1245319b609c089becfcdb
msgid "Auxiliary Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-auxiliary-functions.rst:6
#: 117d730b80384c689ed0eaa7819e18a4
msgid "This page describes how to set up additional features which can be invoked from the transmitter's auxiliary function switches, from Mission Planner using the ``Aux function`` sub-tab of the ``Data`` tab, via MAVLink/Mission command (:ref:`MAV_CMD_DO_AUX_FUNCTION <mav_cmd_do_aux_function>`) or from external :ref:`buttons <common-buttons>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-auxiliary-functions.rst:9
#: c7a0aed9e86d45bf9134a502f4696c71
msgid "Configuring which transmitter channel is used"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-auxiliary-functions.rst:11
#: c9b4f0dcecbb42b69c94ac2f714e8c13
msgid "Any RC input channel can be assigned any auxiliary function. However, the RC channel should not be used by any other function, such as flight mode selection or flight controls. By default, channels 1-6 are used for flight controls (i.e. pitch, roll, vertical, yaw, forward, and lateral), and channels 7 and 8 are used for camera mount gimbal yaw and pitch control. There is no default flight mode channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-auxiliary-functions.rst:14
#: c2339332784b48939aef03d39f76c8a6
msgid "Assigning the Feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-auxiliary-functions.rst:16
#: 250ff66a64ea4c3cbfc9ee5a230302f3
msgid "The ``RCx_OPTION`` parameters control these features. For example, the :ref:`RC7_OPTION <RC7_OPTION>` parameter controls which feature is assigned to RC input 7. Each RC channel has its own ``RCx_OPTION`` parameter that can be accessed in the full parameter list."
msgstr ""

